# Domain Layer Rule

This rule documents the conventions and responsibilities of the Domain Layer in the Mozome Flutter project.

## Scope

- Applies to: `domain/` directory and related files.

## Topics

- Pure Dart business logic (no Flutter dependencies)
- Entities: core business objects
- Use Cases: app logic and business rules
- Abstract Repository: contracts for data access
- App Navigator: navigation contracts
- Domain Config: configuration for domain logic

## Best Practices

- Keep the domain layer framework-agnostic
- No direct dependencies on data or ui layers
- Write unit tests for all business logic
- Use abstract classes for repositories to enforce contract
- Keep entities immutable
- Define clear boundaries between business logic and infrastructure
- Model failures as value objects, not exceptions

